A project `.claude/skilletor.json` declaring `sources.shared = { local: <path> }` merges field-wise into the user source `shared = { git: … }`; origin stays `user`, the backend picks `local`. Result: a cloned repo renders its own templates into the GLOBAL user scope (`~/.claude/skills`) with no trust request (probe 01). Also a trusted project git URL can gain a `local` field and switch backend without renewed trust: `identityOf` prefers git, `makeBackend` picks local (probe 02). Code: src/config.ts:177-180, 341-349; src/engine.ts:133-144, 319-325. Fix direction: resolve sources per scope (a project may not alter a user source), bind trust to the actual backend and its origin.

Repro: probe file by the skilletor-71 audit session, copied to docs-free scratch; reproduced by the orchestrator against exports of e371b13 AND v0.2.0 (pre-existing, not introduced by k62/k63/k65).

